<title>UK: Britain's OFT invites comment on three agreed buys.</title>
<headline>Britain's OFT invites comment on three agreed buys.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Office of Fair Trading, the preliminary regulator of mergers and takeovers, said on Thursday it was inviting comment from interested parties on three agreed acquisitions sealed in late 1996.</p>
<p>The deals are -- retailer Great Universal Stores Plc's planned buy of Experian, Aon Corp's acquisition of Inchcape Plc insurance subsidiary Bain Hogg, and the purchase by Primark Corp of British financial information company ICV.</p>
<p>In each case, representations about any competition or public interest aspects of the deal should be made to the OFT by January 15.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
